==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*keh₂p-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|upheven}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ūpāhebban||to lift up, raise up, exalt, rise in the air, fly}}, equivalent to {{prefix|en|up|heave}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|opheffen||to lift, raise}}, {{cog|de|aufheben||to lift, raise, cancel, repeal}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|past2=uphove|past_ptc2=uphoven}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[heave]] or [[lift]] up; [[raise]] up or [[aloft]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[lift]] or [[thrust]] something [[upward]] [[forcefully]], or be similarly lifted or thrust upward.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be lifted up; [[rise]].

